desc:EON Patchbay
//tags: EON ReaKit swing wired patchbay loopback return
// EON Studios — EON Patchbay
// The return half of Swing's WIRED mode. Swing sends every pad out on its
// channel pair (bank A: pad 1 = channels 3/4 ... pad 16 = 33/34; Pad Banks
// Outputs step 5: bank B/C/D on 39/40, 41/42, 43/44, the ten split-off pads on
// 45..64, the bank pairs' sends on 35..38); the
// user's plugins sit between Swing and this, pinned to a pair; this plugin --
// LAST in the chain -- copies the processed channels into a shared ring
// that Swing drains at the top of its next block, ahead of its master
// section, and zeroes them on the way past so nothing reaches the track output
// twice. One audio buffer of latency, which Swing reports as PDC.
//
// It has no controls. The face is a meter: twenty-nine lanes -- bank A's sixteen
// pads in a 4x4 grid (laid out like Swing's pads), Bank B/C/D, and the ten
// split-off pads' own outputs (Own 1-10, Swing's OUTPUTS names) -- showing what
// is coming back through the loopback, and a lamp that says whether Swing is
// actually reading the ring. Embedded in the TCP/MCP it is the 4x4 and one row of
// the thirteen others. All twenty-nine all the time (the user's decision,
// 2026-10-12): under the old layout the thirteen stay dark. The ring's two send
// columns (35..38) are measured but not drawn: they are no pad's.
//
// The layout is negotiated (rk_swing_patchbay.jsfx-inc, CHANNEL LAYOUT): this
// starts in the old one and moves to the new one when Swing proves it reads it.
//
// link_inst: the Swing's INSTANCE ID, pushed by the bridge when Wired switches
// on and re-stamped by its identity walker; it selects the ring, resolved from
// the registry every block (C-1). link_slot: Swing's registry slot at Wired-on
// (session-volatile), the ring only while no id is set; -1 = none yet (sweep
// PLG19: a fresh Patchbay is PARKED -- it writes no ring -- until the bridge
// links it, instead of stamping slot 0's ring). Neither is a user control.

options:gmem=Swing_Media_Transfer no_meter

slider1:link_slot=-1<-1,15,1>-Instance slot (internal; set by the bridge; -1 = none yet)
slider2:link_inst=0<0,99999999,1>-Link Instance (internal; bridge-set)

in_pin:Return L
in_pin:Return R
in_pin:Pad 1 L
